From 6e7ed75ba6ebbffa408f8bacf3f4085afac53a51
Subject: Depth of field: don't gather sharper samples into a blurred pixel
Origin: https://github.com/robtfm/bevy/commit/6e7ed75ba6ebbffa408f8bacf3f4085afac53a51
Date: 2026-10-15T18:34:22+01:00

The gaussian and bokeh gathers weighted samples by distance only, so a
pixel with a large circle of confusion (the sky, clamped to max_depth) pulled
in colour from sharp, in-focus neighbours and smeared them outward: text and
foliage against the sky grew soft fringes while the same edges against nearby
geometry stayed crisp.

Each sample is now also weighted by the ratio of its own circle of confusion
to the gathering pixel's: full weight for a sample at least as blurred, none
for one less than half as blurred, with a smoothstep between. Samples that
are as blurred or blurrier (far imposters next to the sky) still blend freely,
so the far field keeps its soft silhouettes; only surfaces closer to focus
are kept out of the blur behind them.
